    dict(key='06-act-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — One array: int arr[10], n = 7',
         body='TWO. One array: int arr[10], n = 7.\n  traverse: [21, 23, 19, 25, 24, 22, 20]\n  capacity 10, n = 7, 40 bytes in one block\n  address of arr[3] = base + 3 x 4 = base + 12: computed, not searched',
         narration='Now the same week in one array. [[slnc 400]] We reserve ten places, side by side in memory, and store the seven days in the first seven. [[slnc 400]] So the capacity is ten, and n, the number of elements, is seven. [[slnc 500]] Each element takes four bytes. [[slnc 300]] So the address of element three is the base address, plus three times four.'),
