    dict(key='15-act-5', kind='console', title='Act Five — The bill',
         body='FIVE. The bill.\n  binarySearch on 1,000,000 sorted elements: 20 comparisons\n  linearSearch on 1,000,000: -1 after 1,000,000 comparisons, with O(1) extra space\n  growing 7 to 31: a new array and 7 copies; capacity 31\n  every loop here uses O(1) extra space; the static-array-recursive project writes them recursively\n  already in Java: int[] itself, and java.util.Arrays for fill, copyOf, sort, binarySearch',
         narration='And the bill. [[slnc 400]] On a million sorted elements, binary search needs twenty comparisons. [[slnc 300]] Linear search needs a million. [[slnc 400]] Both are loops, so both use only a few extra variables: order one extra space. [[slnc 500]] And the capacity never changes. [[slnc 300]] To grow from seven to thirty one places, we allocate a new array and copy every element.'),
